'''''Luzula canariensis''''' is a plant species in the genus ''[[Luzula]]'', family [[Juncaceae]]. It is endemic to the [[Canary Islands]] off the northwest coast of Africa. It is a perennial herb {{convert|35|-|90|cm}} tall, with long grass-like leaves.<ref>Poir. in J.&nbsp;B.&nbsp;A.&nbsp;M. de Lamarck, Encycl., Suppl. 3: 532 (1813)</ref><ref>L. Borgen, Check-List Chromos. Macarones. Vasc. Pl. 30 (1977).</ref><ref>[http://juncaceae.e-monocot.org/taxonomy/term/1657 eMonocots]</ref>

